&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Do We Do?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Triple Whale is the AI operating system built for modern ecommerce. We help you see what&#39;s actually working in your business, what&#39;s not, and what to do next. Then we take action for you — pausing the underperforming ad, generating the next batch of creative, flagging the inventory risk before it bites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We pull every signal in your business into one place, and put it on the most trusted measurement foundation in the industry. And on top of that, we give you the most actionable AI in commerce — Moby 2 — letting you tap any LLM you want, grounded in the full context of your business. Moby 2 doesn&#39;t just surface insights, it executes decisions for you, with automations that make the rest of your stack smarter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The result: more than 65,000 brands like Kitsch, OUAI, and True Classic turn mountains of complex data into actions that actually grow profit, at a speed and scale that is not humanly possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;re Applying for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Triple Whale is looking for a Context Engineer to help ecommerce brands successfully adopt Moby, our AI teammate for marketing analysis, planning, and execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a customer-facing activation role for someone with strong performance marketing instincts, practical AI fluency, and the ability to help customers turn Moby into a trusted part of how they work. You will not be the long-term operator inside the customer’s business. Your job is to enable the customer’s own operators - founders, marketers, agencies, and growth teams to use Moby confidently and effectively.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*This is a remote role with a strong preference for candidates based on the West Coast. The person in this role must be able to consistently work Pacific Time (PT) hours.*&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead customer activation for Moby, helping new users identify the first use cases most likely to create value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate each customer’s goals, team structure, marketing motion, and growth challenges into practical Moby workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable customer operators to use Moby in their day-to-day work across paid media, measurement, creative, and growth planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach customers on how to evaluate Moby’s recommendations, ask better questions, and turn AI outputs into decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be prescriptive during onboarding: diagnose opportunities, recommend workflows, and help customers build early trust in Moby.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strategic relationships with customers to help them discover and adopt new Moby use cases over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify repeatable activation patterns and turn them into playbooks the broader team can use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, design, and engineering to share customer feedback and improve the Moby experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience in media buying, growth marketing, ecommerce marketing, or agency strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with platforms such as Meta, Google, TikTok, Amazon, Shopify, Klaviyo, or similar ecommerce/growth tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of marketing metrics like CAC, ROAS, MER, LTV, AOV, contribution margin, retention, and payback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience using AI tools such as Claude, ChatGPT, Perplexity, Cursor, Replit, Lovable, n8n, or similar systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and comfort working directly with founders, marketers, operators, and agencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The confidence to be prescriptive without taking over: you can recommend what to do while teaching the customer how to operate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity, speed, and a collaborative attitude in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agency experience or experience managing multiple brands/accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling DTC or retail brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with attribution, incrementality, MMM, or marketing measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with SQL or BI tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in customer success, solutions consulting, or performance marketing leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base salary for this role is $120,000–$150,000 per year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Eligible employees receive medical coverage; a 401(k) with a company match of up to 3%; 30 days of paid time off accrued monthly after the first 30 days of employment; five sick days; and nine paid company holidays. Triple Whale also offers paid parental leave for eligible employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Triple Whale is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Us in Making Waves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for more than just a job and want to be part of a movement reshaping the future of Ecommerce, Triple Whale is the place for you. We’re on the lookout for driven, curious, and creative individuals ready to thrive in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Referred?&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;Got here thanks to a friend? Splash some gratitude their way!&amp;nbsp; They&#39;ll need to submit your application through our referral system to make it official.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Step&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Step&#39;s mission is to improve the financial future of the next generation. Millions of people use our banking and borrowing products to manage, build, and grow their money. Now that we&#39;re part of Beast Industries – the company behind MrBeast – we&#39;re poised for a new phase of growth to deliver financial literacy and tools at massive scale.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Marketing at Step runs on data. Every acquisition channel, lifecycle campaign, rewards drop, and measurement decision depends on clean, connected, well-modeled data flowing between our product, our warehouse, and a dozen marketing platforms. Today, much of that work lands on engineering. We&#39;re hiring a Director, Marketing Technology, to own it end-to-end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a deeply technical, hands-on role for someone with a software or data engineering background who wants to apply that skill set to growth. You&#39;ll be the architect and operator of Step&#39;s marketing technology stack: owning our ad channel and attribution integrations, managing our vendor ecosystem (Segment, AppsFlyer, Braze, Funnel, and others), building the data models and analytical tooling the marketing team runs on, and shipping the monthly rewards and offers that drive engagement. You&#39;ll act as the bridge between Marketing, Product, and Engineering taking on the technical work that currently pulls engineers away from the core product, and raising the bar on what marketing can measure, automate, and personalize.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll start as a hands-on individual contributor with the opportunity to build and lead a marketing technology team as the function scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the marketing technology stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the architecture, roadmap, and day-to-day operation of Step&#39;s martech ecosystem including CDP, MMP, lifecycle messaging, data aggregation, and analytics tooling along with the documentation, QA, and governance standards that keep it reliable and privacy-compliant&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage all marketing technology partners (Segment, AppsFlyer, Braze, Funnel, and similar), including evaluation, implementation, optimization, and contract/renewal input&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and optimize ad channel and measurement integrations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure, validate, and maintain integrations with paid channels (Meta, Google, TikTok, and similar), including server-side conversion APIs, event schemas, setup counting methods, attribution windows, and first-party audience syncs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own attribution and mobile measurement (AppsFlyer/Segment): SKAN/postback configuration, conversion windows, deduplication, and channel-level data quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner on GA4 implementation including event taxonomy, funnel conversion configuration, and custom reporting; leveraging GA4 data to fill attribution gaps across channels and inform incrementality analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the data backbone of the marketing team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the pipelines and data models that power marketing reporting, audience segmentation, and campaign measurement&amp;nbsp; with identity, event, and audience definitions kept consistent across product, warehouse, and activation platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop self-serve analytical tools, dashboards, and automations so marketers can answer their own questions (ie. spend pacing, funnel conversion, LTV, incrementality)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ship marketing programs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical build of Step&#39;s monthly rewards and offers program end to end targeting logic, delivery, tracking, and post-campaign readout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support lifecycle and CRM campaign execution in Braze: triggers and data feeds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner across the company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as marketing&#39;s technical counterpart to Product, Engineering, and Data scoping requests, setting priorities, and taking build work off engineering&#39;s plate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You might thrive in this role if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years across software engineering, data engineering, or marketing technology, with meaningful time spent as a hands-on engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience owning a modern martech stack at a consumer company: CDP (Segment or similar), MMP (AppsFlyer, Adjust, or Branch), and lifecycle platforms (Braze or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL and working proficiency in a scripting language (Python or JavaScript); comfortable with APIs, webhooks, event-driven architectures, and cloud data warehouses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of mobile and web attribution: conversion APIs, SKAdNetwork, postbacks, deduplication, and incrementality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear communicator who bridges marketing, engineering, and executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are hungry for action and you&#39;d rather ship a working solution this week than a perfect one next quarter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating martech at larger scale, ideally through viral moments or campaign-driven traffic spikes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some of the technology we use:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kotlin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;gRPC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protocol Buffers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dagger&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Postgres&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JOOQ&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BigQuery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Terraform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Remote (US) or San Mateo, CA, with occasional travel for team offsites and key meetings&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Chief Marketing Officer&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you don&#39;t meet every single qualification. Strong candidates rarely check every box, and we&#39;d rather meet you than miss you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We stand for the side hustlers, the creators, the freelancers, and the investors — people who are not afraid to take on challenges, especially when it comes to their finances. Step is focused on disrupting the banking industry by delivering a differentiated, mobile-first consumer experience, and we operate like the customers we serve: customer obsessed, acting as owners, moving with urgency, and breaking the norm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Step is a wholly owned subsidiary of&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Beast Industries&lt;/strong&gt;, the media and entertainment company founded by Jimmy Donaldson (MrBeast), the most-watched person in the world. Beast Industries spans digital media, consumer products, philanthropy, and new ventures, with an audience reach no consumer company has ever had — and Step is tasked with turning that reach into financial literacy and tools for the next generation at massive scale. With Beast&#39;s distribution and brand behind it, Step is positioned to scale significantly over the next 12 months, and joining now means helping shape that trajectory from the inside.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Step is a remote-first company building banking for the next generation. We offer competitive compensation and stock options, generous medical, dental, vision, and company-paid life insurance, a 401k plan with Safe Harbor company matching, a flexible vacation policy and paid company holidays, 12 weeks paid parental leave with flexible return to work, and a company-provided technology package. If you&#39;re looking to join a fast-growing company with a strong mission and vision that puts people first, we want to meet you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Step is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Step is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities throughout the application and interview process. If you need an accommodation, please let us know at people@step.com and we&#39;ll work with you to provide appropriate support.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

